-- title:
--   Theorem 12.4 — Online boosting regret bound (normalized WOCL losses, corrected constants $8nGDT/(\gamma^{3/2}\sqrt N)$)
-- statement:
--   **Statement (Theorem 12.4, corrected).** Let $K\subseteq\mathbb R^n$ ($n\ge1$) be convex with $0\in K$ and diameter at most $D$, let $f_1,\dots,f_T:\mathbb R^n\to\mathbb R$ be convex and $G$-Lipschitz, $\gamma\in(0,1]$, $N\ge1$, and let $H\subseteq\{a\}\to K$ be nonempty. Run Algorithm 36 with $\kappa=G$, $\delta=\sqrt{D^2/(\gamma N)}$, $\eta_i=\min\{2/i,1\}$ and weak learners $W^1,\dots,W^N$ predicting in $K$, each a $\gamma$-WOCL for $H$ on its stage losses $f^i_t(x)=\nabla\hat f_t(x^{i-1}_t)\cdot x$ normalized by $\hat GD=2GD$ (so that their range on $K$ is at most $1$), with regret $\mathrm{Regret}_T(W)$. Then for every $h^\star\in\mathrm{CH}(H)$ — in particular the best hypothesis in the convex hull in hindsight —
--   $$\sum_{t=1}^{T}f_t(x_t)-\sum_{t=1}^{T}f_t(h^\star(a_t))\;\le\;\frac{8nGDT}{\gamma^{3/2}\sqrt N}+\frac{2GD}{\gamma}\mathrm{Regret}_T(W).$$
--
--   **Formalization Note.** Three corrections. (i) The retired statement applied the WOCL hypothesis to the un-normalized stage losses; Definition 12.1 only constrains $W$ on linear losses of range $\le1$ over $K$, so for $GD>1/2$ the hypothesis was vacuous and $\mathrm{Regret}_T(W)$ unconstrained (refuted with a negative value). As in the book's proof ("the following equivalent restatement of the WOCL guarantee"), the WOCL guarantee is now assumed on $f^i_t/(\hat GD)$ with $\hat G=2G$, the Lipschitz constant of the extended losses $\hat f_t=S_\delta[f_t+G\,\mathrm{Dist}(\cdot,K)]$; the comparator in `IsGammaWOCL` (module `_v2`) is the real infimum over $H$. (ii) The losses are convex and $G$-Lipschitz on all of $\mathbb R^n$ (§12.3's standing assumption), replacing the gradient-bound idiom that was vacuous at points of non-differentiability; $0\in K$ (the starting point $x^0_t=0$) and $W^i(a_t)\in K$ are explicit. (iii) The printed first term $5nGDT/(\gamma\sqrt N)$ is not supported by the book's proof even after (i): Lemma 12.3's constant is $2\delta G$ (not $\delta G$), $f_t+G\,\mathrm{Dist}(\cdot,K)$ is $2G$-Lipschitz so $\hat f_t$ is $2nG/\delta$-smooth by Lemma 2.8 (not $nG/\delta$), and with $\delta=D/\sqrt{\gamma N}$ the chain $\sum_tf_t(x_t)-f_t(x^\star_t)\le\sum_t\hat f_t(x^N_t)-\hat f_t(x^\star_t)+4\delta GT$ (using $f\le\hat f$ on $K$) and Lemma 12.5 give $4\delta GT+\frac{2\beta D^2T}{\gamma^2N}=\frac{4GDT}{\sqrt{\gamma N}}+\frac{4nGDT}{\gamma^{3/2}\sqrt N}\le\frac{(4+4n)GDT}{\gamma^{3/2}\sqrt N}$; the bound stated here is this derived bound rounded up to $8n$. The conclusion is stated for every $h^\star\in\mathrm{CH}(H)$, which is equivalent to the book's $\min_{h^\star\in\mathrm{CH}(H)}$. The run predicate is `IsOnlineBoostingRun` of the re-issued `OnlineConvexOpt_OnlineBoosting_Algorithm_v2` (unchanged, importing `OnlineConvexOpt_FirstOrder_Protocol_v2` for the projection).
-- source:
--   Hazan, Introduction to Online Convex Optimization, 2nd ed., arXiv:1909.05207v3, p. 200, Theorem 12.4 (PDF p. 222) — corrected transcription: WOCL applied to the stage losses normalized by ĜD = 2GD (as in the proof, Algorithm 36 line 10 omits the normalization), and first term 8nGDT/(γ^{3/2}√N) in place of the printed 5nGDT/(γ√N), which the proof does not support (Lemma 12.3's constant is 2δG and f̂_t is 2nG/δ-smooth)

import Mathlib
import Definitions.Def_OnlineConvexOpt_OnlineBoosting_Algorithm_v2
import Definitions.Def_OnlineConvexOpt_OnlineBoosting_WOCL_v2

namespace OnlineConvexOpt.OnlineBoosting

/-- Theorem 12.4, "Main" (Hazan, *Introduction to Online Convex Optimization*, 2nd ed.,
arXiv:1909.05207v3, p. 200, PDF p. 222), with corrected constants. The predictions `x_t`
generated by Algorithm 36 (with `κ = G`, `δ = √(D²/(γN))`, `η_i = min{2/i,1}`, `N ≥ 1` weak
learners that are `γ`-WOCL for `H`, run on convex `G`-Lipschitz losses `f_t : ℝⁿ → ℝ` over a
convex decision set `K ∋ 0` of diameter `≤ D`) satisfy, for every `h⋆ ∈ CH(H)` (in particular
the best hypothesis in the convex hull of `H` in hindsight),
`∑_{t=1}^T f_t(x_t) - ∑_{t=1}^T f_t(h⋆(a_t)) ≤ 8nGDT/(γ^{3/2}√N) + (2GD/γ)Regret_T(W)`.

As in the book's proof, the WOCL guarantee of the `i`-th weak learner is applied to the stage
losses `f^i_t` normalized by `ĜD = 2GD` (the Lipschitz constant `Ĝ ≤ 2G` of the extended
losses times the diameter), so that their range over `K` is at most `1`, Definition 12.1's
precondition; `H ⊆ {a} → K` is nonempty and the weak learners predict in `K`.

Corrected version. (i) The retired statement applied the WOCL hypothesis to the un-normalized
stage losses, whose range over `K` exceeds `1` as soon as `GD > 1/2`, making the hypothesis
vacuous and `Regret_T(W)` unconstrained (the book's Algorithm 36 line 10 omits the `1/(ĜD)`
normalization its proof uses). (ii) The losses are now `G`-Lipschitz and convex on `ℝⁿ` (the
retired gradient-bound idiom was vacuous at points of non-differentiability). (iii) The printed
bound `5nGDT/(γ√N)` is not supported by the book's own proof even after (i): Lemma 12.3's
constant is `2δG` (not `δG`), the extended loss `f_t + G·Dist(·,K)` is `2G`-Lipschitz so by
Lemma 2.8 `f̂_t` is `2nG/δ`-smooth (not `nG/δ`), and with `δ = D/√(γN)` the proof yields
`4δGT + 2βD²T/(γ²N) = 4GDT/√(γN) + 4nGDT/(γ^{3/2}√N) ≤ (4+4n)GDT/(γ^{3/2}√N)`; the bound stated
here, `8nGDT/(γ^{3/2}√N)`, is this derived bound rounded up. -/
theorem online_boosting_regret_v2
    {n : ℕ} (hn : 0 < n)
    (K : Set (EuclideanSpace ℝ (Fin n))) (hKconv : Convex ℝ K)
    (h0K : (0 : EuclideanSpace ℝ (Fin n)) ∈ K)
    (D G : ℝ) (hDpos : 0 < D) (hGpos : 0 < G) (hD : ∀ x ∈ K, ∀ y ∈ K, dist x y ≤ D)
    (γ : ℝ) (hγpos : 0 < γ) (hγ1 : γ ≤ 1)
    (N T : ℕ) (hN : 0 < N) (hT : 0 < T)
    (δ : ℝ) (hδ : δ = Real.sqrt (D ^ 2 / (γ * N)))
    (η : ℕ → ℝ) (hη : ∀ i : ℕ, 1 ≤ i → η i = min (2 / (i : ℝ)) 1)
    (A : Type*) (a : ℕ → A) (H : Set (A → EuclideanSpace ℝ (Fin n))) (hHne : H.Nonempty)
    (hHK : ∀ h ∈ H, ∀ c : A, h c ∈ K)
    (f : ℕ → EuclideanSpace ℝ (Fin n) → ℝ) (hfconv : ∀ t, ConvexOn ℝ Set.univ (f t))
    (hfG : ∀ t, ∀ x y, |f t x - f t y| ≤ G * dist x y)
    (W x : ℕ → ℕ → EuclideanSpace ℝ (Fin n)) (hW : ∀ t i, W t i ∈ K)
    (fstage : ℕ → ℕ → EuclideanSpace ℝ (Fin n) → ℝ)
    (xplay : ℕ → EuclideanSpace ℝ (Fin n))
    (hrun : IsOnlineBoostingRun K γ δ G N T η a f W x fstage xplay)
    (RegretBoundW : ℝ)
    (hWOCL : ∀ i : ℕ, 1 ≤ i → i ≤ N →
      IsGammaWOCL K γ T a H (fun t => W t i) (fun t y => fstage t i y / (2 * G * D))
        RegretBoundW)
    (hstar : A → EuclideanSpace ℝ (Fin n)) (hstar_mem : hstar ∈ convexHull ℝ H) :
    (∑ t ∈ Finset.Icc 1 T, f t (xplay t)) - ∑ t ∈ Finset.Icc 1 T, f t (hstar (a t)) ≤
      (8 * n * G * D * T) / (γ ^ (3 / 2 : ℝ) * Real.sqrt N) + (2 * G * D / γ) * RegretBoundW := by
  sorry

end OnlineConvexOpt.OnlineBoosting
